WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.521
Equity Detective teaches a practical workflow for reading a company from its financial statements.

2
00:00:07.521 --> 00:00:11.604
Here is the workflow in brief, using a fictional company.

3
00:00:13.005 --> 00:00:16.456
Start with the profit and loss statement.

4
00:00:16.456 --> 00:00:21.170
Our fictional company has revenue of one thousand crore.

5
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:26.389
After operating costs, EBITDA is one hundred and eighty crore.

6
00:00:26.389 --> 00:00:33.039
Subtract depreciation, interest and tax, and net profit is about seventy crore.

7
00:00:34.439 --> 00:00:36.250
Next, follow the cash.

8
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:42.259
Operating cash flow adds back depreciation, which used no cash this year,

9
00:00:42.259 --> 00:00:46.127
and subtracts money tied up in working capital.

10
00:00:46.127 --> 00:00:49.008
That gives about one hundred crore.

11
00:00:49.008 --> 00:00:55.594
After eighty crore of capital expenditure, free cash flow is under twenty crore.

12
00:00:56.994 --> 00:00:58.735
Then the balance sheet.

13
00:00:58.735 --> 00:01:02.067
Assets always equal liabilities plus equity.

14
00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:06.610
Profit that is not paid out as dividends is added to equity,

15
00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:11.683
and the cash-flow statement explains every rupee of change in cash.

16
00:01:13.083 --> 00:01:16.363
Ratios turn these numbers into questions.

17
00:01:16.363 --> 00:01:19.323
An EBITDA margin of eighteen percent,

18
00:01:19.323 --> 00:01:26.523
cash conversion of about one hundred and forty-three percent, and debt of half the equity.

19
00:01:26.523 --> 00:01:30.763
Each ratio is a prompt to investigate, not a verdict.

20
00:01:32.163 --> 00:01:36.470
Ask whether profit is turning into cash, what drives growth,

21
00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:42.572
how much debt there is and at what cost, and how the company compares with its peers.

22
00:01:43.972 --> 00:01:48.113
In the course you will practise this with interactive labs,

23
00:01:48.113 --> 00:01:52.324
including a three-dimensional model of the three statements,

24
00:01:52.324 --> 00:01:55.904
and finish with an evidence-backed research report.

25
00:01:55.904 --> 00:01:58.782
This is education, not investment advice.

